{{Hiero/2cartouche|align=right|era=mk|name=Senusret III|praenomen=<hiero>F12-s-D21:t-z:#:n</hiero>|nomen=<hiero>ra-N28-D28*D28:D28</hiero>}} '''Senusret III''' was a [[pharaoh]] of [[Ancient Egypt|Egypt]]. He ruled from [[1878 BC]] to [[1839 BC]], and was the fifth monarch of the [[Twelfth dynasty of Egypt|Twelfth Dynasty]]. His pyramid was constructed at [[Dahshur]]. He was a Great Pharaoh of the 12th Dynasty and continued his Kingdom's expansion deep into Nubia where he erected massive River Forts at Uronarti. A papyrus in the [[Berlin]] Museum shows Year 20 of his reign is equivalent to Year 1 of his son [[Amenemhat III]]. This means that he initiated a coregency with his son in this year. A stone block recovered ''in situ'' from the ruins of his Funerary Temple at Abydos suggests that he was still alive in his 39th Regnal Year. This implies that he served as the senior coregent in his son's reign for almost 2 decades prior to his death.
